>For a creamy texture</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">large</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Eggs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For binding the ingredients</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Honey</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional, for a touch of sweetness</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Dry Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Self-rising flour</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adds the perfect fluffiness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Baking powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Helps with the rise</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Enhances flavor</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Toppings</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Sesame seeds or poppy seeds</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional, adds a nice crunch</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-4699-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"4699\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking sheet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Line with parchment paper</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 large bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing wet ingredients</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Rolling Pin&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For shaping the dough</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-4699-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-4699-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"4699\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Mix Wet Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-1-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">In a large bowl, whisk together the cottage cheese, eggs, and honey until smooth.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Combine Dry Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-2-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Add the self-rising flour, baking powder, and salt; stir until a soft dough forms.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Shape the Dough</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-3-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Lightly flour your work surface and divide the dough into 6 equal pieces.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Form the Bagels</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-4-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Roll each piece into a rope about 6 inches long, then join the ends to form a bagel shape.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Place on Baking Sheet</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-5-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Place the formed bagels on the prepared baking sheet.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Add Toppings</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-6-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">If desired, brush the tops with a little beaten egg and sprinkle with seeds.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Bake</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-7-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Bake for 20–25 minutes, or until golden brown.</div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Cool and Serve</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4699-step-8-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Cool slightly before serving.</div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-4699-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>3g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>8g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up some delicious Cottage Cheese Bagels with these simple ingredients!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Cottage-Cheese-Bagels.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for cottage cheese bagels displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-4697\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Cottage-Cheese-Bagels.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Cottage-Cheese-Bagels-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Cottage cheese</strong> – 1 cup, for a creamy texture</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Self-rising flour</strong> – 2 cups, adds the perfect fluffiness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Large eggs</strong> – 2, for binding the ingredients</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Baking powder</strong> – 1 teaspoon, helps with the rise</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon, enhances flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Honey</strong> – 1 tablespoon (optional), for a touch of sweetness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sesame seeds or poppy seeds</strong> – for topping (optional), adds a nice crunch</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-cottage-cheese-bagels\"><strong>How to Make Cottage Cheese Bagels</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up some delightful cottage cheese bagels! With a preparation time of about 10 minutes and a cooking time of 20-25 minutes, these bagels are perfect for a quick breakfast or snack. Allow a little extra time for cooling before serving.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-Make-Amazing-Cottage-Cheese-Bagels-1.webp\" alt=\"Illustrative guide on how to make amazing cottage cheese bagels, featuring the combination of ingredients, shaping of the dough, and final preparation for baking.\" class=\"wp-image-4706\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-Make-Amazing-Cottage-Cheese-Bagels-1.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-Make-Amazing-Cottage-Cheese-Bagels-1-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Mix the Wet Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a large bowl, whisk together the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottage_cheese\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cottage cheese</a>, eggs, and honey until smooth.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Combine Dry Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the self-rising flour, baking powder, and salt; stir until a soft dough forms.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Shape the Dough</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Lightly flour your work surface and divide the dough into 6 equal pieces.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Form the Bagels</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Roll each piece into a rope about 6 inches long, then join the ends to form a bagel shape.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Place on Baking Sheet</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the formed <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bagels </a>on the prepared baking sheet.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Add Toppings</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If desired, brush the tops with a little beaten egg and sprinkle with seeds.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Bake</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bake for 20–25 minutes, or until golden brown.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Cool and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cool slightly before serving.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Breakfast</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>35 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with your favorite toppings!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-cottage-cheese-bagels\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Cottage Cheese Bagels</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Opt for low-fat cottage cheese for a lighter bagel.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in herbs or spices for added flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the dough rest for a few minutes for better texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brush with egg wash for a golden crust.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with toppings like seeds or cheese for variety.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-cottage-cheese-bagels\"><strong>How to Serve this Cottage cheese bagels</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Spread with avocado and sprinkle with chili flakes for a spicy kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with smoked salmon and capers for a gourmet touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Slather on some cream cheese and add fresh cucumber slices.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a dollop of your favorite jam for a sweet twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a side of fresh fruit for a balanced breakfast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a warm bowl of soup for a comforting lunch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to keep your cottage cheese bagels fresh and delicious:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Cottage Cheese Bagels Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow bagels to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap each bagel in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped bagels in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Cottage Cheese Bagels</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap each cooled bagel tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped bagels in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For best quality, avoid stacking bagels directly on top of each other.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Cottage Cheese Bagels</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For refrigerated bagels, toast them in a toaster or oven until warm.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For frozen bagels, thaw overnight in the fridge before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a toaster oven or regular oven at 350°F (175°C) for about 10 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with your favorite toppings for the best flavor!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Is cottage cheese good for bagels?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Cottage cheese adds a wonderful creaminess and moisture to bagels, enhancing their texture and flavor. It also provides a good source of protein, making your bagels more nutritious and satisfying.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Can you use cottage cheese instead of yogurt in bagels?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, you can substitute cottage cheese for yogurt in bagel recipes. While the texture may differ slightly, cottage cheese will still provide moisture and a rich flavor. Just blend it well to achieve a smoother consistency if desired.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How do you make Bethenny Frankel&#8217;s viral cottage cheese bagel?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make Bethenny Frankel&#8217;s viral cottage cheese bagel, mix cottage cheese with an egg and some flour to form a dough. Shape it into a bagel and bake until golden. You can top it with your favorite seasonings or spreads for added flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Why do bodybuilders eat cottage cheese before bed?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Bodybuilders often eat cottage cheese before bed because it is high in casein protein, which digests slowly. This slow release of protein helps to support muscle recovery and growth overnight, making it a popular choice for those looking to build muscle mass.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making cottage cheese bagels is not just a recipe; it&#8217;s a delightful experience! Picture the warm, cheesy aroma filling your kitchen as you bake. These bagels are simple, rewarding, and perfect for any time of day. So, roll up your sleeves, get creative, and enjoy every bite of your homemade goodness. Happy baking!</p>\n",
